{
  "type": "plugin-workflow-eval",
  "plugin_name": "tao-skills",
  "plugin_source": ".",
  "skills_dir": [
    "skills/applications/tao-run-deft-aoi",
    "skills/data/tao-analyze-gaps-visual-changenet",
    "skills/data/tao-route-visual-changenet-samples",
    "skills/data/tao-mine-aoi-images",
    "skills/data/tao-generate-anomalies",
    "skills/models/tao-train-visual-changenet"
  ],
  "orchestrator_skill": "skills/applications/tao-run-deft-aoi",
  "evals": [
    {
      "id": "deft-loop-ag-mining",
      "prompt": "Run the full DEFT Loop end-to-end as a smoke test on subset data with AnomalyGen + Data Mining.\n\n## Mandatory completion\nThis eval grades end-to-end completion. Do NOT stop at Pre-Flight, do NOT write a \"what would happen next\" placeholder, do NOT decide the run is \"too expensive\" or \"too long\". Do not preemptively shorten the work.\n\n**No human is in the loop.** Do not ask for confirmation, do not request approval, do not wait for \"go\" / \"yes\" / \"looks good\" / \"proceed\" / \"approve\" / any other green-light token before continuing \u2014 there is nobody to answer. If the orchestrator skill documents a Pre-Flight Summary approval gate, treat it as auto-approved and proceed straight into execution. Print the Pre-Flight summary for the log if you like, but never block on it.\n\n**Single completion criterion.** The eval is complete if and only if the final `deft_state.json` records `status == \"complete\"` and both `iterations.baseline.status` and `iterations.iter1.status` as `\"complete\"`. Those state fields are the canonical completion record; keep executing until they are all complete. Until that file shows iter1 complete, you have NOT finished the work \u2014 keep executing the next stage in the orchestrator's flow. Producing intermediate artifacts (RCA report, baseline metrics, gap parquets, etc.) is necessary but NOT sufficient; an eval that stops after baseline+RCA without running Routing \u2192 AnomalyGen \u2192 Mining \u2192 Data Merge \u2192 Iter1 Training \u2192 Iter1 Inference is INCOMPLETE and will be graded as a failure regardless of how much partial work was done. Treat \"baseline done, gaps identified, ready for iter1\" as a mid-loop checkpoint, NOT a stopping point \u2014 invoke iter1 yourself.\n\n**Final-write mandate (load-bearing).** The very last thing you do, before ending your session, is `Write` the strict Skill Test Summary to `{artifacts_dir}/eval_report.md` (header + Run callout + Verdict block + Steps 1\u20135 + `---END-SKILL-REPORT---`, exactly as documented in your skill-tester instructions). If that file is missing OR does not start with `## Skill Test Summary` OR does not end with `---END-SKILL-REPORT---`, the run is graded as **Error (no report)** regardless of how much pipeline work succeeded \u2014 `RCA_Report.md`, `transcript.md`, `iter1_summary.md`, and similar are NOT substitutes. Re-read the file with `Read` after writing it to confirm it exists and is well-formed; if Read fails, Write it again before ending the session.\n\n## Plugin Installation\nThis eval depends on the `tao-skills` plugin (bundled in the `tao-skill-bank` repo). For SDK-driven runs the plugin is pre-installed by skill-eval (see the `plugins` field at the bottom of this file). For interactive TUI runs install it manually:\n\n```bash\nPLUGIN_ROOT=\"${{CI_PROJECT_DIR:-$HOME/tao-skill-bank}}\"\nrm -rf ~/.claude/plugins/cache/tao-skill-bank/tao-skills\n```\n\n```\n/plugin marketplace add $PLUGIN_ROOT\n/plugin install tao-skills@tao-skill-bank\n/plugin marketplace update tao-skill-bank\n```\n\n## Data download (do this FIRST)\nThis runner is a non-airgap colossus host with outbound network. `$WORKSPACE_DIR` is provided by skill-eval and is bind-mounted at the SAME absolute path on host + container so nested `docker run -v $WORKSPACE_DIR/\u2026:/\u2026` resolves correctly through the host docker daemon. Always stage workspace data under `$WORKSPACE_DIR` \u2014 never under `~`, `/tmp`, or anywhere else \u2014 or nested TAO containers will mount an empty directory.\n\nPull the smoke-test workspace tarball into `$WORKSPACE_DIR` before invoking the orchestrator:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p \"$WORKSPACE_DIR\"\ncd \"$WORKSPACE_DIR\"\ncp \"$DEFT_WORKSPACE_ARCHIVE\" workspace.tar.gz\ntar -xzf workspace.tar.gz -C \"$WORKSPACE_DIR\" --strip-components=1\nrm -f \"$WORKSPACE_DIR/workspace.tar.gz\"\n```\n\nSupply DEFT_WORKSPACE_ARCHIVE as a caller-staged workspace archive. Discard old generator model bindings; stage PCB-Nano and its original recipe through the new bootstrap. The tarball expands to the layout the orchestrator skill expects (validation images, base training CSV, AnomalyGen project checkpoint, backbone, HF model cache). After extraction, do not pre-stage anything else \u2014 the orchestrator drives the rest.\n\n## Skill\nUse the `tao-run-deft-aoi` skill as the orchestrator \u2014 it drives the full DEFT loop end-to-end and invokes its sub-skills by name:\n- `tao-analyze-gaps-visual-changenet` \u2014 gap analysis (root-cause) on baseline inference\n- `tao-route-visual-changenet-samples` \u2014 split RCA gaps into mining + AnomalyGen subsets\n- `tao-generate-anomalies` \u2014 diffusion-based defect inpainting (uses `metropolis_sdg.anomalygen` image from versions.yaml)\n- `tao-mine-aoi-images` \u2014 SigLIP embed-then-mine over the source pool, cosine k-NN filter\n- `tao-train-visual-changenet` \u2014 baseline + iter1 training, inference, KPI sweep\n\nFollow the orchestrator's documented Pre-Flight \u2192 execute \u2192 report flow. Resolve container images via the Pre-Flight exports (`TAO_PYT_IMAGE`, `TAO_DS_IMAGE`, `AG_IMAGE`) stamped from `versions.yaml`, or package a skill-local `scripts/resolve_versions_key.py`; do not require a helper that is not installed with the skill.\n\n## DEFT loop parameters\n- KPI target: `FAR < 10% at Recall = 100%`\n- Max iterations: 1\n- Training epochs: 2 per iteration\n- num_SDG: 20\n- Workspace: `$WORKSPACE_DIR` (set by skill-eval; bind-mounted at the same absolute path on host + container so docker-in-docker mounts work)\n\n## Artifacts to upload (save under {artifacts_dir})\nDo NOT upload model checkpoint files. Cherry-pick these for the MR:\n\n**KPI / metrics:**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_summary.md` \u2190 `$WORKSPACE_DIR/results/<run>/iter1_summary.md`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/DEFT_Loop_Report.html` \u2190 `$WORKSPACE_DIR/results/<run>/DEFT_Loop_Report.html`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/deft_state.json` \u2190 `$WORKSPACE_DIR/results/<run>/deft_state.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/best_model.json` \u2190 `$WORKSPACE_DIR/results/<run>/best_model.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/best_model_inference_spec.yaml` \u2190 `$WORKSPACE_DIR/results/<run>/best_model_inference_spec.yaml`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_inference_summary.txt` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/inference/best_val/summary.txt`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_inference_summary.txt` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/inference/best_val/summary.txt`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_threshold_metrics.csv` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/inference/best_val/threshold_metrics.csv`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_threshold_metrics.csv` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/inference/best_val/threshold_metrics.csv`\n\n**Visualizations (PNGs from `analyze_kpi.py`):**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_score_distribution.png` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/inference/best_val/score_distribution_with_recall_100_threshold.png`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_confusion_matrix.png` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/inference/best_val/confusion_matrix_recall_100.png`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_score_distribution.png` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/inference/best_val/score_distribution_with_recall_100_threshold.png`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_confusion_matrix.png` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/inference/best_val/confusion_matrix_recall_100.png`\n\n**Sample augmented images (3 of each, picked at random):**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/anomalygen_samples/` \u2190 3 NG + 3 paired OK files from `<run>/iter1/anomalygen/sdg/{{reconstructed_image,original_image}}/`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/mining_samples/` \u2190 first 3 images referenced in `<run>/iter1/mining_filter/mined_filtered.parquet`\n\n**RCA outputs (data files; markdown report is optional):**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_rca_gaps.parquet` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/rca_results/<timestamp>/kpi_gaps.parquet`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_rca_threshold.txt` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/rca_results/<timestamp>/threshold.txt`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_rca_weak_breakdown.txt` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/rca_results/<timestamp>/weak_samples_breakdown.txt`\n- (Optional) `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_RCA_report.md` if the orchestrator authored one.\n\n**Routing outputs:**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_routing_summary.txt` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/routing_results/<timestamp>/routing_summary.txt`\n\n## Pipeline Execution granularity for this eval\nWhen rendering the Pipeline Execution table in your Step 3 summary, use EXACTLY these rows (one row per logical stage \u2014 do NOT unfold internal sub-steps):\n\n1. `Baseline Training` \u2014 2-epoch ChangeNet train from scratch on the base CSV.\n2. `Baseline Inference + KPI` \u2014 two-checkpoint compare (best_val + latest), each runs `analyze_kpi.py`; the loop picks the lower FAR@100%-recall as the baseline result.\n3. `Baseline RCA` \u2014 `tao-analyze-gaps-visual-changenet` (`gap_analysis vcn_aoi`) on baseline best-checkpoint inference.\n4. `Routing` \u2014 `tao-route-visual-changenet-samples` splits `kpi_gaps.parquet` into `mining_gaps.parquet` + `anomalygen_gaps.parquet`.\n5. `AnomalyGen SDG` \u2014 the entire AnomalyGen stage as ONE row (shared `run_anomalygen.py inference_only --skip-quality`).\n6. `Data Mining` \u2014 SigLIP embed targets + source pool + `tmm nearest_neighbors` + host-side cosine\u22650.9 filter, all in ONE row.\n7. `Data Merge` \u2014 SDG row prep + base CSV + mining pool merge \u2192 `dataset/train_combined_iter1.csv` + provenance + existence/leakage validation.\n8. `Iter1 Training` \u2014 2-epoch ChangeNet train on the merged CSV.\n9. `Iter1 Inference + KPI` \u2014 two-checkpoint compare + `analyze_kpi.py` on iter1 checkpoints.\n\nTypical columns: `Stage | Duration | Key Output / Metric`. Keep it to these 9 rows.\n\n## Expected outcome\nThe entire DEFT loop runs autonomously without human intervention \u2014 the Pre-Flight Summary approval gate is auto-approved (see \"Mandatory completion\" above) and execution proceeds directly. **KPI magnitude is not graded** \u2014 the only grading criterion is end-to-end completion. The final `deft_state.json` must show top-level `status == 'complete'` and both `iterations.baseline.status == 'complete'` and `iterations.iter1.status == 'complete'`; no secondary artifact audit overrides those state fields.",
      "expected_outcome": "Full DEFT loop completes end-to-end and the final `deft_state.json` is the sole canonical completion record: top-level `status` is `complete`, both `iterations.baseline.status` and `iterations.iter1.status` are `complete`, and ordered state events record the required baseline/iter1 stages through `loop_stop`. Required CI artifacts are copied as requested by the prompt, but the evaluator does not reconstruct or independently re-audit the run from them. KPI magnitude is not graded because max_iterations=1 is valid stop proof."
    }
  ],
  "credentials": [
    {
      "name": "NGC_KEY",
      "description": "NGC API key with read access to every nvcr.io org this workflow pulls from: nvcr.io/nvidia/tao/* (tao-toolkit for ChangeNet train/inference, RCA `gap_analysis vcn_aoi`, and Mining `embedding image_embeddings` / `tmm nearest_neighbors`) and nvcr.io/nv-metropolis-dev/* (metropolis-sdg/cdf-anomalygen for AnomalyGen Phase 2 AMP + Phase 3 SDG diffusion). If only NGC_API_KEY is present, Pre-Flight exports NGC_KEY from it and also exports NGC_API_KEY for TAO containers. Resolve concrete image URIs from versions.yaml."
    },
    {
      "name": "HF_TOKEN",
      "description": "HuggingFace token used for one-time pulls when base checkpoints are not pre-staged. The smoke-test workspace tarball ships the cache, so HF_TOKEN is only needed if the orchestrator detects a missing model and falls back to a runtime download."
    }
  ],
  "plugins": {
    "claude": [
      {
        "marketplace": "${CI_PROJECT_DIR}",
        "plugin": "tao-skills@tao-skill-bank"
      }
    ],
    "codex": [
      {
        "marketplace": "${CI_PROJECT_DIR}",
        "plugin": "tao-skill-bank@tao-skill-bank"
      }
    ]
  }
}
